[36m(main_task pid=1120327)[0m Doc 2(Title: Bactris) Bactris Bactris is a genus of spiny palms which is native to the Mexico, South and Central America and the Caribbean. Most species are small trees about tall, but some are large trees while others are shrubs with subterranean stems. Species of Bactris are spiny-stemmed, spiny-leafed palms in the tribe Rynchosporieae of the palm family Arecaceae. The genus Bactris is a pantropical genus of spiny palms, which is native to the Americas. The genus has more than 70 species, and is native to Mexico, southern Texas, and Central America, and the Caribbean. As of 2020, the genus includes more than 70 species, but only a handful have been subjected to taxonomic study.
