[36m(main_task pid=1120327)[0m Doc 2(Title: "Jonathan Groff") Jonathan Groff Jonathan Drew Groff (born March 26, 1985) is an American actor and singer. Groff rose to prominence in 2006 for his performance in the lead role of Melchior Gabor in the original Broadway production of ""Spring Awakening"", for which he was nominated for the Tony Award for Best Actor in a Musical. He originated the role of Jonah Barringer in the off-Broadway production of "Red" in 2009, for which he won a Lucille Lortel Award. In 2010, he starred in the feature film "What Would Norman Conner Do?" (2010) and had a recurring role as Hugo Schuchhardt in the television series "Bob's Burgers". In 2013, he played the title role in the Broadway musical "Dear Evan Hansen", for which he won a Tony Award for Best Actor in a Musical. He played Benjamin Franklin in the 2014 film "Paul Revere's Day" (2014). He originated the role of Carson Horne in the musical "Jagged Little Pill". On April 7, 2018, he began his first principal role in the off-Broadway musical "Altar Boyz", for which he was nominated for the Lucille Lortel Award for Best Actor in a Musical. He originated the role of Roger Mills in the 2019 musical "The Ferryman", for which he was nominated for the Drama Desk Award for Featured Actor in a Musical and won a Lucille Lortel Award for Best Featured Actor in a Musical. He originated the role of Nathan Hale in the 2021 musical "The Difference". He originated the role of Justice Stewart in the 2022 musical "Herod Josiah". He played Calvin Simms in the 2019 film "Being Atlantic". He originated the role of Mark Walbeck in the 2021 musical "Wake Me When It's Over". </documents>
