[36m(main_task pid=1120327)[0m Doc 2(Title: Accelerant) Accelerant Accelerants are substances that can bond, mix or disturb another substance and cause an increase in the speed of a natural, or artificial chemical process. Accelerants play a major role in chemistry—most chemical reactions can be hastened with an accelerant. Accelerants alter a chemical bond, speed up a chemical process, or bring organisms back to homeostasis. Accelerants are not necessarily catalysts as they may be consumed by the process. In fire protection, the term accelerant is used very broadly to include any substance or mixture that ""accelerates"" a fire's progress, rather than, say, merely wetting, cooling, absorbing or neutralizing the fire.
