[36m(main_task pid=1120327)[0m Doc 2(Title: "New York, Westchester and Boston Railway") as the IRT Dyre Avenue Line ( train) of the New York City Subway. In 1871 the Southern Westchester Railroad was incorporated to run from what was then the southern edge of Westchester County (now the Bronx) at the Harlem River to the Westchester county seat, White Plains, along the same general route as was taken by the New York, Westchester and Boston Railway. In 1912 the New York, Westchester and Boston Railway Company was incorporated to continue the line from Mount Vernon to the Bronx and later extended from Mount Vernon to the city terminal in Riverdale in the Bronx. The city terminal was in the village of Riverdale, Bronx.</documents>
