[36m(main_task pid=1120327)[0m Doc 2(Title: "Mona Leaves-a") Mona Leaves-a ""Mona Leaves-a"" is the nineteenth episode of ""The Simpsons""<nowiki>'</nowiki> nineteenth season. It originally aired on the Fox network in the United States on May 11, 2008. The episode features the death of Homer's mother, Mona Simpson. Homer is reunited with his mother, Mona, but is not willing to forgive her for all the times she left him as a child. When she dies, a guilt-ridden Homer refuses to stop crying, and a distraught Bart thinks her death has caused her son's death. In the end, Homer accepts that his mother died for his own good, as she was abusive, leaving Bart as a child to raise himself. The episode reveals that the teenage Homer was a fling with Mona, resulting in Lisa. The episode marks the first appearance of the character Andy, who would appear throughout the season. Mona's death is later referenced in the episode "Secret Santas", where Marie tries to "get rid" of Leslye because of her laziness, and Lisa says she never had a mother like Mona.</nowiki> </documents>
