[36m(main_task pid=1120327)[0m Doc 2(Title: "Heart sounds") Heart sounds Heart sounds are the noises generated by the beating heart and the resultant flow of blood through it. Specifically, the sounds reflect the turbulence created when the heart valves snap shut. In cardiac auscultation, an examiner may use a stethoscope to listen for these unique and distinct sounds that provide important auditory data regarding the condition of the heart. In healthy adults, there are two normal heart sounds, often described as a ""lub"" and a ""dub"": lub is systolic and can be heard early in ventricular systole ("") while dub is a diastolic sound and can be heard a split second later. Audibly dub is the second sound of the heartbeat.</documents>
