[36m(main_task pid=1120327)[0m Doc 2(Title: Prohibition) uses. Alcohol consumption was never illegal under federal law. Nationwide Prohibition did not begin in the United States until January 1920, when the Eighteenth Amendment to the U.S. Constitution went into effect. The 18th amendment was ratified in 1919, and was repealed in December 1933 with the ratification of the Twenty-first Amendment. Concern over excessive alcohol consumption began during the temperance movement of the 1830s, and the movement gained strength as the transatlantic telegraph made information about alcohol-related problems spread widely. Temperance activists began calling for an end to alcohol sales in 1880, and succeeded in 1919, when the 18th Amendment passed. </documents>
