[36m(main_task pid=1120327)[0m Doc 2(Title: "Not Going Out") Out"" began on 8 March 2018. In Series 9, two episodes were classically farcical: in Stolen, Lee and Lucy, having broken into their best friends' house, are forced to hide under their bed when their friends return unexpectedly early - and head straight for the bedroom; in Pants on Fire, lies build upon lies, and embarrassment is the name of the game. A live Christmas-based episode will be broadcast on BBC One on 21 December 2018. The series focuses on Lee Mack, who plays a fictional version of himself: an unambitious man in his late thirties living as a lodger in a flat in the London Docklands. Originally from Chorley, Lancashire (which is approximately 20 miles from Southport, Mack's real-life birthplace), Lee is a negligent, unmotivated layabout. Frequently between jobs, he spends most of his days on his sofa, smoking, watching sport (which he watches at a technical level only, as if he is the host of a TV programme), and drinking. In his work-related episodes, Lee attempts to adapt to his workplace, such as a promotional committee, by submitting fictional work-related ideas (including the sketchy idea of working as a librarian at a charity auction event - prescient for a BBC commission now) and by miscommunication – yet he ultimately fails. He is always punctual for his gigs (which begin at 8pm), despite his antics. (Nick Frost & Simon Pegg feature as himself in Lee's family project – a family comedy.) Two episodes were never filmed, and they are a mystery as to whether they will ever air. Lucy's death in Series 3 had a major impact on the series, which prompted Lee to change his work/life balance and focus on his personal life (where he actively plays God). This series focused on his relationship with his mother.</documents>
